  "note": "Per plan, the modules that end WAITING (parked on a browser nobody drives) on the runner; gate.py tolerates WAITING only for these, so a module absent from the list that parks is a regression. How this seed was built: every module conformance/baseline.json names, minus those the 2026-09-08 runs (no SPA, no browser) show finishing without one: discovery-end-point-verification, par-attempt-invalid-http-method, ensure-response-type-code-idtoken-fails and ensure-response-type-token-fails (PASSED or WARNING there), plus, in private_key_jwt, the five par-*-jwt-client-assertion / audience modules (also PASSED or WARNING there). The same set is applied to the self-signed plan, which shares the modules but whose 2026-09-08 run failed earlier. Everything else needs an authorization code or an authorization-endpoint visit, and one of them (ensure-unsigned-authorization-request-without-using-par-fails) was seen WAITING. Modules whose PAR-level behaviour could not be confirmed from the tree (par-ensure-pkce-required, par-plain-pkce-rejected, ensure-request-object-without-redirect-uri-fails, the dpop and client-assertion negatives) are listed, so the seed errs towards tolerating a park rather than failing the first real run; re-recording tightens it. oidcc-basic-static is not listed: fapi-conformance.yml does not run it, so a gate over that plan treats every WAITING as a regression until it is recorded.",
